[27.5945, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[6B\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;246m\u276f \u001b[38;5;231mJudge the five hackathon entries with Verdict. Work only in this folder. The entries are \u001b[39m         \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mentries/receipt-run.md, entries/common-room.md, entries/tidewatch.md, entries/menu-match.md and \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mentries/plant-pal.md. create_rubric with the YAML text of hackathon-judging.yaml (read it and \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mpass its contents), then compare the five entries (one subject per file, named after the entry's \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mtitle, each a file input). Then, without judging again, re-rank the same evaluations twice with \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mthe reaggregate tool (evaluationIds: all five, persist: true): first with { \"method\": \"min\" } \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m(weakest link), then with { \"method\": \"formula\", \"formula\": \"impact_n * 0.5 + originality_n * \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m0.5\" } (moonshot). Finally print a WINNERS table: aggregation, winner, score, and how many judge \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mcalls the re-ranking needed.\u001b[39m                                                                      \r\u001b[4B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;174m\u273d\u001b[3GLevitating\u001b[38;5;216m\u2026\u001b[38;5;174m \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;244m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u250